== Episodes ==

=== Episode 1: Cake ===
The first episode is Cake Week.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a45268155/great-british-bake-off-weekly-themes/|title=GBBO 2023: What themes are they doing each week this year?|date=22 September 2023|website=Cosmopolitan}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/great-british-bake-off-national-weeks-cancelled-newsupdate/|title=Great British Bake Off scraps national-themed weeks|website=Radio Times}}</ref> For the first signature challenge, the bakers were given two hours to produce a Vertical Layer Cake made of sponge and icing. For the technical challenge, set by Paul, the bakers were tasked with making "The Great British Bake Off Cake" (the one seen in the credits each week<ref>{{cite web |last1=Agius |first1=Nicola |title=Great British Bake Off fans want Channel 4 to fix this opening credits 'gaffe' |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a837346/great-british-bake-off-opening-credits-error-missing-raspberry/ |website=Digital Spy |publisher=Hearst UK |access-date=18 April 2024 |date=6 September 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Mitchell |first1=Harriet |title=Great British Bake Off premiere's challenge featured big Easter egg |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a45328504/bake-off-2023-premiere-missing-raspberry-cake/ |website=Digital Spy |publisher=Hearst UK |access-date=18 April 2024 |date=26 September 2023}}</ref>) in two hours, comprising two layers of moist chocolate sponge covered with chocolate ganache and fresh raspberries. A 3D cake replica of an animal of the bakers' choosing was set as the showstopper; the bakers were given four hours, the judges expecting the bake to be mostly sponge.
