==Specials==

Two specials were commissioned for the festive season:<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvzoneuk.com/post/gbbo-festive2023 |title=BAKE OFF REVEALS RETURNING BAKERS FOR FESTIVE SPECIALS ON CHANNEL 4|date=6 December 2023|work=TV Zone UK|accessdate=7 December 2023}}</ref>	

=== ''The Great Christmas Bake Off'' ===
The Great Christmas Bake Off featured [[The Great British Bake Off (series 8)|Series 8]] winner [[Sophie Faldo]], Dan Beasley-Harling from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 9)|Series 9]], Amelia Le Bruin from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 10)|Series 10]], Linda Rayfield from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 11)|Series 11]], George Aristidou from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 12)|Series 12]], and Carole Edwards from [[The Great British Bake Off (series 13)|Series 13]].

For the signature challenge, the bakers had to make 12 [[Mince Pie|mince pies]] using any pastry, with a festive filling, in 2 hours. The technical challenge, set by Paul, was a tear and share cinnamon snowflake bread, with an enriched dough, in 2¾ hours. The showstopper challenge, was to bake an exquisite celebration cake based on redemption, with any style and flavours, in 4 hours.
